 "designNotes": [
  "⚠️ SHIELDS EXIST NOW, AND THEY DIDN'T. Zero in the game against 19 authored defensive logics. Every tradition gets shield forms — including the ones whose 'shield' is a bracer, a board, or a wrap.",
  "⚠️ STILLHOLD MAKES THE BEST SHIELDS AND THE WORST WEAPONS, on purpose. That is the tradition expressed as gear rather than asserted in prose, and it is the clearest test that this grammar is doing its job.",
  "EVERY TRADITION HAS A TAIL VARIANT, per the modes-and-tails pass. A Grave-Caller's knife, a Maw blade, a Smotherer's cord. THE TAIL IS NOT A BETTER ITEM — it is the same form with different tags, because a tail is a different answer to what the craft is FOR, not more power.",
  "TAGS COME FROM THE TRADITION, NOT THE FORM. A blade is melee+edge whoever made it; what makes it ashwarden is death+quiet. Once Track B's matcher lands, that makes carrying gear that suits your craft mechanically real — which is the whole reason to generate any of this.",
  "AND THE NAMING PATTERNS ARE DELIBERATELY PLAIN. 'A Pale Long Knife' and 'the Redline Spear' — no invented proper nouns, because a generator that invents names invents lore, and the engine's own rule is that it must not."
 ]
}
